					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-1186646#post-2293784</guid>
				<title>(no title)</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-1186646/operation-camp-granada#post-2293784</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Wed, 13 May 2015 12:42:02 +0000</pubDate>
								<wikidot:authorUserId>1324229</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>Neat. While I think that the action itself would have worked much better as a narrative tale rather than an AAR, the additional e-mail stuff was quite interesting.</p> <p>My only complaint is with the first e-mail. The guy says &quot;if [w] was [x], then [y] was [z]&quot; enough times that it becomes weird.<sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-998078-1" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" >1</a></sup> Also, the bit about Iris at the end seemed like an afterthought of &quot;oh wait, right, she's supposed to be anomalous,&quot; given that up until that point, the guy had been rhapsodizing about her shooting skills.</p> <p>Minor issues, but an overall +1</p> <div class="footnotes-footer"> <div class="title">Footnotes</div> <div class="footnote-footer" id="footnote-998078-1"><a href="javascript:;" >1</a>. I checked and he only says it twice. I guess that twice is enough for that construction to sound weird.</div> </div> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
